## React Patterns

### Component Structure

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Functional component with typed props
interface Props {
  userId: string;
  onSuccess?: () => void;
}

export function UserProfile({ userId, onSuccess }: Props) {
  const { data, isLoading } = useUser(userId);

  if (isLoading) return <Skeleton />;
  if (!data) return <NotFound />;

  return <div>{data.name}</div>;
}
```

### Hook Usage

```typescript
// ✅ Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
// ✅ Use useCallback for callbacks passed to children
// ✅ Use useMemo for expensive computations
// ✅ Use React.memo for pure components (only after profiling)
```

---

## Import Order

1. React / Framework imports
2. Third-party libraries
3. Internal imports (absolute paths)
4. Relative imports
5. Type imports

```typescript
import { useState } from 'react';
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui';
import { User } from './types';
import type { Config } from './config';
```

---

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase | `UserProfile` |
| Hooks | camelCase + use | `useUserData` |
| Utilities | camelCase | `formatDate` |
| Constants | SCREAMING_SNAKE | `MAX_RETRIES` |
| Types/Interfaces | PascalCase | `UserProps` |
| Files (components) | PascalCase | `UserProfile.tsx` |
| Files (hooks/utilities) | camelCase | `useUserData.ts` |

---

## Anti-Patterns

| ❌ Don't | ✅ Do |
|---------|-------|
| `any` | `unknown` or specific types |
| Non-null assertion `!` | Proper null checks |
| `as` casting | Type guards |
| Inline object types | Interfaces/Types |
| Default exports | Named exports |
